//
// The core's call to the overlay is a direct jump to the slot, and nothing is
// linked behind it.
//
// This is the cheapest test in the suite and it pins the whole mechanism. A
// `link_with` entry becomes an INPUT() in the generated linker script, and
// ld.lld parses an input it does not recognise as a script -- which is how
// slot.ld gets to define `overlay_entry` as an absolute address with no body.
// If that ever stops working the symbol acquires a definition somewhere and the
// core calls it, quietly, instead of jumping into the slot.
//
// Two independent facts, because either alone can hold while the mechanism is
// broken: the symbol must be ABS (no section, no body), and the call site must
// be an immediate jump to the slot address rather than an indirect one.
//
// REQUIRES: peano
//
// RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
// RUN: %PEANO_INSTALL_DIR/bin/clang++ --target=aie2p-none-unknown-elf -O2 -c %S/../resident.cc -o %t/resident.o
// RUN: %python %S/../pm.py emit --recipe one_slot --slot-ld %t/slot.ld --phases 0 --out %t/d.mlir
// RUN: cd %t && %aiecc --tmpdir=%t/p1 --get-xclbin --xclbin-name=%t/p1.xclbin --get-npu-insts --npu-insts-name=%t/p1.bin %t/d.mlir
//
// Absolute, sized 0, and in no section: the linker never found a body for it.
// RUN: %PEANO_INSTALL_DIR/bin/llvm-readelf -s %t/p1/elfs_main_core_0_2/elfs_main_core_0_2.elf | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SYM
// SYM: 00002000 {{ *}}0 NOTYPE {{ *}}GLOBAL {{ *}}DEFAULT {{ *}}ABS overlay_entry
//
// And the call really is a jump to that address.
// RUN: %PEANO_INSTALL_DIR/bin/llvm-objdump -d %t/p1/elfs_main_core_0_2/elfs_main_core_0_2.elf | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=JUMP
// JUMP: jl {{.*}}#0x2000
//
// The slot fragment itself: symbol assignments, and nothing else. A fragment
// that grew a SECTIONS command would collide with the generated script rather
// than being merged into it.
//
// It used to also carry an ASSERT keeping the resident out of the slot, which
// meant the only thing between a growing resident and the core overwriting its
// own code was a side effect of how lld treats an unrecognised input. That is
// now the core's program_memory_reserved attribute, which shortens the linker's
// program region -- so the absence of the ASSERT here is the point, not an
// omission.
// RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LD --input-file=%t/slot.ld
// LD: overlay_entry = 0x2000;
// LD-NOT: ASSERT
//
// The reservation is what enforces the boundary now, and it is on the core.
// RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RESV --input-file=%t/d.mlir
// RESV: program_memory_reserved = 8192
